\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Covariance agreement and the transfer trace}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{The equality in \ref{fdip-00FT} is an equality of centered
Gaussian laws on the circle: the two fields have the same
covariance function. \citet{Corollary 4.4}{klein1981periodic}
states that the only periodic Gaussian OS-positive processes
on the line with the two-sided Markov property on the circle
are the periodic Ornstein-Uhlenbeck processes up to a positive
constant factor. The finite transfer operator of \ref{fdip-007S} is
diagonalized by Hermite functions when the weight and the mass
are positive and the time step is one. Its trace on a periodic
chain equals the corresponding finite partition function. That
finite diagonalization is the transfer statement available
here. The covariance identity is separate from a limit of
those operators.}
